Austria moves to open its online gambling market to multiple licences

Austria's parliamentary Finance Committee has approved a reform that would replace the current closed system with multiple online gambling licences, iGaming Business reports. Licences could be issued from January 1, 2027, with licensed operations starting on October 1, 2027. Operators active without an Austrian licence would have to stop by the end of 2026 to qualify. The package adds a central exclusion register, deposit limits across providers, a €5 maximum stake per slot game and powers to block illegal sites and payments. Lawyers still expect final approval before Christmas, after Malta's objection extended the EU review to December 7.

